add a case for `ParamSpecExpr` similar to how other node types are handled.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/python__mypy__0.920/mypy/server/astdiff.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n    else:\\n        # Other node types are handled elsewhere.\\n        assert False, type(node)\\n\", \"new_text\": \"\\n    elif isinstance(node, ParamSpecExpr):\\n        return ('ParamSpecExpr', common,\\n                node.variance,\\n                snapshot_type(node.upper_bound))\\n    else:\\n        # Other node types are handled elsewhere.\\n        assert False, type(node)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [str_replace_editor]:\nThe file /workspace/python__mypy__0.920/mypy/server/astdiff.py has been edited. Here's the result of running `cat -n` on a snippet of /workspace/python__mypy__0.920/mypy/server/astdiff.py:\n   220\t        symbol_table = snapshot_symbol_table(prefix, node.names)\n   221\t        # Special dependency for abstract attribute handling.\n   222\t        symbol_table['(abstract)'] = ('Abstract', tuple(sorted(node.abstract_attributes)))\n   223\t        return ('TypeInfo', common, attrs, symbol_table)\n   224\t    elif isinstance(node, ParamSpecExpr):\n   225\t        return ('ParamSpecExpr', common,\n   226\t                node.variance,\n   227\t                snapshot_type(node.upper_bound))\n   228\t    else:\n   229\t        # Other node types are handled elsewhere.\n   230\t        assert False, type(node)\n   231\t\n   232\t\n   233\tdef snapshot_type(typ: Type) -> SnapshotItem:\n   234\t    \"\"\"Create a snapshot representation of a type using nested tuples.\"\"\"\nReview the changes and make sure they are as expected. Edit the file again if necessary."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I have updated the `snapshot_definition` function in `astdiff.py` to handle `ParamSpecExpr` nodes. Now, let's create a script to reproduce the error and verify that the changes resolve the issue. We'll simulate the conditions that lead to the crash by creating a minimal example that uses `ParamSpecExpr`.\n\nLet's create a script named `reproduce_error.py` to test this.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/workspace/python__mypy__0.920/reproduce_error.py\", \"content\": \"\\nfrom mypy.nodes import ParamSpecExpr\\nfrom mypy.server.astdiff import snapshot_definition\\n\\n# Create a dummy ParamSpecExpr node\\nparam_spec_expr = ParamSpecExpr('P', 'module.P', None, 0)\\n\\n# Create a common tuple for snapshot\\ncommon = ('module.P', 'kind', True)\\n\\n# Attempt to create a snapshot of the ParamSpecExpr node\\nsnapshot = snapshot_definition(param_spec_expr, common)\\n\\nprint('Snapshot created successfully:', snapshot)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [str_replace_editor]:\nFile created successfully at: /workspace/python__mypy__0.920/reproduce_error.py"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /workspace/python__mypy__0.920/reproduce_error.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "EXECUTION RESULT of [execute_bash]:\npython /workspace/python__mypy__0.920/reproduce_error.py\r\nTraceback (most recent call last):\r\n  File \"/workspace/python__mypy__0.920/reproduce_error.py\", line 11, in <module>\r\n    snapshot = snapshot_definition(param_spec_expr, common)\r\n  File \"/testbed/mypy/server/astdiff.py\", line 224, in snapshot_definition\r\n    elif isinstance(node, ParamSpecExpr):\r\nNameError: name 'ParamSpecExpr' is not defined[Python Interpreter: /opt/miniconda3/envs/testbed/bin/python]\nroot@openhands-workspace:/workspace/python__mypy__0.920 # \n[Command finished with exit code 1]"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "The error indicates that `ParamSpecExpr` is not defined in the context of the `reproduce_error.py` script. This is because we need to import `ParamSpecExpr` from the correct