\n- [x] Bug fix\r\n- [ ] New feature\r\n- [ ] Documentation / docstrings\r\n- [ ] Tests\r\n- [ ] Other\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I've run the latest [black](https://github.com/psf/black) with default args on new code.\r\n- [ ] I've updated CHANGELOG.md and CONTRIBUTORS.md where appropriate (see note about typos above).\r\n- [x] I've added tests for new code.\r\n- [x] I accept that @willmcgugan may be pedantic in the code review.\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\nPromptBase.on_validate_error() should explicitly ask for markup in case the console passed to it has markup disabled globally.\r\n\r\nFixes #3881."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll localize with the graph tools first, starting from the symbols named in the issue.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"search_similar_code\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"on_validate_error\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"on_validate_error\",\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rich/prompt.py\",\n   \"line\": 258,\n   \"kind\": \"definition\"\n  }\n ]\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "on_validate_error is defined in rich/prompt.py. Checking its callers and callees before reading any file.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_neighbors\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"on_validate_error\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "rich_3882", "repo": "Textualize/rich", "base_commit": "4d6d631a3d2deddf8405522d4b8c976a6d35726c", "files": ["rich/prompt.py"], "symbols": ["on_validate_error", "pre_prompt"], "n_hunks": 1, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_prompt.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live to