aking in to account the spans.  Basically it would replace tabs with unstyled spaces. This resolves that issue by extending the style(s) on the tab to cover the new space characters\r\n\r\n<img width=\"623\" alt=\"Screenshot 2023-07-28 at 22 00 06\" src=\"https://github.com/Textualize/rich/assets/554369/28c170a0-b154-4a81-af17-a8a334bebd3a\">\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "I'll localize with the graph tools first, starting from the symbols named in the issue.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"search_similar_code\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"right_crop\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"right_crop\",\n \"matches\": [\n  {\n   \"file\": \"rich/text.py\",\n   \"line\": 86,\n   \"kind\": \"definition\"\n  }\n ]\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "right_crop is defined in rich/text.py. Checking its callers and callees before reading any file.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_neighbors\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"right_crop\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "{\n \"symbol\": \"right_crop\",\n \"callers\": [\n  \"extend\",\n  \"Text\",\n  \"__init__\"\n ],\n \"callees\": [\n  \"extend\",\n  \"Text\",\n  \"__init__\"\n ],\n \"note\": \"neighbors derived from symbols co-occurring in the patch\"\n}"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Getting the surrounding call graph so I read only the files that matter.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"get_code_subgraph\", \"arguments\": {\"symbol\": \"right_crop\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "rich_3061", "repo": "Textualize/rich", "base_commit": "aca9467ec6a482b3bed1ba7d2e3de72271c5f817", "files": ["rich/text.py"], "symbols": ["right_crop", "extend", "Text", "__init__"], "n_hunks": 13, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_panel.py", "tests/test_text.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": 