ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\u2796 Drop support for `pydantic.v1`\n\n\u2796 Drop support for `pydantic.v1`\r\n\r\nWhen trying to use a `pydantic.v1` model with FastAPI, an error is raised."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/dependencies/utils.py (hunk at line 375).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/dependencies/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"        fastapi_annotations = [\\n            arg\\n            for arg in annotated_args[1:]\\n            if isinstance(arg, (FieldInfo, may_v1.FieldInfo, params.Depends))\\n        ]\\n        fastapi_specific_annotations = [\\n            arg\", \"new_text\": \"        fastapi_annotations = [\\n            arg\\n            for arg in annotated_args[1:]\\n            if isinstance(arg, (FieldInfo, params.Depends))\\n        ]\\n        fastapi_specific_annotations = [\\n            arg\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/dependencies/utils.py (hunk at line 384).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/dependencies/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"                arg,\\n                (\\n                    params.Param,\\n                    temp_pydantic_v1_params.Param,\\n                    params.Body,\\n                    temp_pydantic_v1_params.Body,\\n                    params.Depends,\\n                ),\\n            )\\n        ]\\n        if fastapi_specific_annotations:\\n            fastapi_annotation: Union[\\n                FieldInfo, may_v1.FieldInfo, params.Depends, None\\n            ] = fastapi_specific_annotations[-1]\\n        else:\\n            fastapi_annotation = None\\n        # Set default for Annotated FieldInfo\\n        if isinstance(fastapi_annotation, (FieldInfo, may_v1.FieldInfo)):\\n            # Copy `field_info` because we mutate `field_info.default` below.\\n            field_info = copy_field_info(\\n                field_info=fastapi_annotation,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\\n                annotation=use_annotation,\\n            )\\n            assert field_info.default in {\\n                Undefined,\\n                may_v1.Undefined,\\n            } or field_info.default in {RequiredParam, may_v1.RequiredParam}, (\\n                f\\\"`{field_info.__class__.__name__}` default value cannot be set in\\\"\\n                f\\\" `Annotated` for {param_name!r}. Set the default value with `=` instead.\\\"\\n            )\", \"new_text\": \"                arg,\\n                (\\n                    params.Param,\\n                    params.Body,\\n                    params.Depends,\\n                ),\\n            )\\n        ]\\n        if fastapi_specific_annotations:\\n            fastapi_annotation: Union[FieldInfo, params.Depends, None] = (\\n                fastapi_specific_annotations[-1]\\n            )\\n        else:\\n            fastapi_annotation = None\\n        # Set default for Annotated FieldInfo\\n        if isinstance(fastapi_annotation, FieldInfo):\\n            # Copy `field_info` because we mutate `field_info.default` below.\\n            field_info = copy_field_info(\\n                field_info=fastapi_annotation,  # type: ignore[arg-type]\\n                annotation=use_annotation,\\n            )\\n            assert (\\n                field_info.default == Undefined or field_info.default == RequiredParam\\n            ), (\\n                f\\\"`{field_info.__class__.__name__}` default value cannot be set in\\\"\\n                f\\\" `Annotated` for {param_name!r}. Set the default value with `=` instead.\\\"\\n            )\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_14609", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "1b3bea8b6be2220cc1544653ea785d2134fcb35b", "files": ["docs_src/request_form_models/tutorial002_pv1_an_py39.py", "docs_src/request_form_models/tutorial002_pv1_py39.py", "fastapi/_compat/__init__.py", "fastapi/_compat/main.py", "fastapi/_compat/may_v1.py", "fastapi/_compat/model_field.py", "fastapi/_compat/shared.py", "fastapi/_compat/v1.py", "fastapi/_compat/v2.py", "fastapi/datastructures.py", "fastapi/dependencies/utils.py", "fastapi/encoders.py", "fastapi/exceptions.py", "fastapi/openapi/models.py", "fastapi/openapi/utils.py", "fastapi/param_functions.py", "fastapi/params.py", "fastapi/routing.py", "fastapi/temp_pydantic_v1_params.py", "fastapi/utils.py"], "symbols": ["FormData", "login", "get_cached_model_fields", "_is_undefined"], "n_hunks": 92, "n_files": 20, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_compat.py", "tests/test_compat_params_v1.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 104, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 36, "tool": "edit_file", "est_tokens": 1807, "split_from": "fastapi_14609"}}
{"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "# Coder \u2014 system prompt\n\nYou are an offline autonomous Python coding agent working in /workspace, a\nrepository snapshot at the commit just before the fix. You resolve one\nissue per session: diagnose the bug or feature request, write the\nsmallest patch that makes the hidden tests pass, and submit it.\n\nThe hidden tests are applied AFTER your patch in a clean container. Test\nfiles and runner config are reset there, so editing them here is wasted\nwork and stripped from your patch. Fix library code only.\n\n## Hard rules\n\n- NEVER edit, create, or delete test files or runner config: tests,\n  conftest, pytest.ini, pyproject.toml, tox.ini, setup.cfg, and any\n  packaging or test-runner file. If a fix seems to need a test change,\n  you are wrong: re-read the issue and the library code.\n- NEVER write scratch scripts, repro scripts, or temp files under\n  /workspace: anything left there enters the patch diff. Scratch work\n  goes under /tmp only, and is deleted before submit.\n- Minimal patches only: change the fewest lines that fix the issue,\n  preserve existing style and names, do not refactor, do not add\n  features the issue does not ask for.\n- Never guess an API or symbol: read the code first.\n- Do not browse the network: there is none. All tools are offline.\n\n## Workflow (follow in order, do not skip steps)\n\n1. READ THE TASK. Extract: what fails, the exact error or wrong\n   behaviour, and any failing test names mentioned in the issue.\n2. LOCALIZE (graph first). Call the code_analyzer sub-agent once with\n   the issue text and the failing test names. Then use the graph tools\n   yourself on the SYMBOLS it returns (never natural-language queries):\n   search_similar_code for symbol lookup, get_code_neighbors for\n   callers and callees, get_code_subgraph for the surrounding call\n   graph. Only then read_file the 1-3 files that matter. Skim, do not\n   dump whole files: read_file returns at most 150 lines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\ud83d\udc1b Fix evaluating stringified annotations in Python 3.10\n\nI've bumped into the exact same issue as https://github.com/tiangolo/typer/discussions/598 so I solved it like https://github.com/tiangolo/typer/pull/721  :smile: \r\n\r\nI'll try to add tests soon but if you can do it faster, please feel free !!"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_11355.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_11355 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom fastapi.dependencies.utils import get_flat_params  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix evaluating stringified annotations in Python 3.10 I've bumped into the exact same issue as https://github.com/tiangolo/typer/discussions/598 so I solved it like https://github.com/tiangolo/typer...\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", get_flat_params)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_11355.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: \ud83d\udc1b Fix evaluating stringified annotations in Python 3.10 I've bumped into the exact same issue as https://github.com/tiangolo/typer/discussions/598 so I solved it like https://github.com/tiangolo/typer..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/dependencies/utils.py (hunk at line 1).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/dependencies/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"import dataclasses\\nimport inspect\\nfrom contextlib import AsyncExitStack, contextmanager\\nfrom copy import copy, deepcopy\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\", \"new_text\": \"import dataclasses\\nimport inspect\\nimport sys\\nfrom contextlib import AsyncExitStack, contextmanager\\nfrom copy import copy, deepcopy\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/dependencies/utils.py (hunk at line 192).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/dependencies/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n\\ndef get_typed_signature(call: Callable[..., Any]) -> inspect.Signature:\\n    signature = inspect.signature(call)\\n    unwrapped = inspect.unwrap(call)\\n    globalns = getattr(unwrapped, \\\"__globals__\\\", {})\\n    typed_params = [\", \"new_text\": \"\\n\\ndef get_typed_signature(call: Callable[..., Any]) -> inspect.Signature:\\n    if sys.version_info >= (3, 10):\\n        signature = inspect.signature(call, eval_str=True)\\n    else:\\n        signature = inspect.signature(call)\\n    unwrapped = inspect.unwrap(call)\\n    globalns = getattr(unwrapped, \\\"__globals__\\\", {})\\n    typed_params = [\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/dependencies/utils.py (hunk at line 221).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/dependencies/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n\\ndef get_typed_return_annotation(call: Callable[..., Any]) -> Any:\\n    signature = inspect.signature(call)\\n    unwrapped = inspect.unwrap(call)\\n    annotation = signature.return_annotation\\n\", \"new_text\": \"\\n\\ndef get_typed_return_annotation(call: Callable[..., Any]) -> Any:\\n    if sys.version_info >= (3, 10):\\n        signature = inspect.signature(call, eval_str=True)\\n    else:\\n        signature = inspect.signature(call)\\n    unwrapped = inspect.unwrap(call)\\n    annotation = signature.return_annotation\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_11355", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "811fa898752e7f5697733a2958ff79ad8dfb5276", "files": ["fastapi/dependencies/utils.py"], "symbols": ["get_flat_params", "get_typed_signature", "get_typed_annotation", "get_typed_return_annotation"], "n_hunks": 3, "n_files": 1, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 0, "test_target": ["tests/test_stringified_annotations_simple.py"], "test_target_source": "test_patch", "synthesized": {"graph_observations": true, "repro_observations": true, "test_observations": true, "read_observations": "snapshot", "reasoning_text": true, "repro_script": "generic"}, "note": "Programmatic replay of the reference patch; graph/repro/test observations are synthesized from patch context, not live tool outputs. Read-file observations are snapshot.", "turns": 13, "generator": "gen_programmatic.py v1", "traj_turn": 8, "tool": "edit_file", "est_tokens": 1858, "split_from": "fastapi_11355"}}
