t": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_rich_3676.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for rich_3676 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom rich.default_styles import _SyntaxError  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# Notes Add support for Exception.__notes__\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", _SyntaxError)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_rich_3676.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: Notes Add support for Exception.__notes__"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in rich/default_styles.py (hunk at line 121).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"rich/default_styles.py\", \"old_text\": \"    \\\"traceback.exc_value\\\": Style.null(),\\n    \\\"traceback.offset\\\": Style(color=\\\"bright_red\\\", bold=True),\\n    \\\"traceback.error_range\\\": Style(underline=True, bold=True, dim=False),\\n    \\\"bar.back\\\": Style(color=\\\"grey23\\\"),\\n    \\\"bar.complete\\\": Style(color=\\\"rgb(249,38,114)\\\"),\\n    \\\"bar.finished\\\": Style(color=\\\"rgb(114,156,31)\\\"),\", \"new_text\": \"    \\\"traceback.exc_value\\\": Style.null(),\\n    \\\"traceback.offset\\\": Style(color=\\\"bright_red\\\", bold=True),\\n    \\\"traceback.error_range\\\": Style(underline=True, bold=True, dim=False),\\n    \\\"traceback.note\\\": Style(color=\\\"green\\\", bold=