ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "fix(panel): fix title missing panel background\n\n Fix `Panel` title missing the panel background style.\r\n    \r\nThis really just reverts the change in 7a38204. There's a history of issues related to the panel title styles, so I was careful to run all the examples in those issues to ensure there wasn't any regression.\r\n    \r\nFixes #3569\r\n\r\n## Type of changes\r\n\r\n- [x] Bug fix\r\n- [ ] New feature\r\n- [ ] Documentation / docstrings\r\n- [ ] Tests\r\n- [ ] Other\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [x] I've run the latest [black](https://github.com/psf/black) with default args on new code.\r\n- [x] I've updated CHANGELOG.md and CONTRIBUTORS.md where appropriate.\r\n- [x] I've added tests for new code.\r\n- [x] I accept that @willmcgugan may be pedantic in the code review.\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_rich_3718.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: fix(panel): fix title missing panel background Fix `Panel` title missing the panel background style. This really just reverts the change in 7a38204. There's a history of issues related to the panel ti..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in rich/panel.py (hunk at line 146).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"rich/panel.py\", \"old_text\": \"            Padding(self.renderable, _padding) if any(_padding) else self.renderable\\n        )\\n        style = console.get_style(self.style)\\n        partial_border_style = console.get_style(self.border_style)\\n        border_style = style + partial_border_style\\n        width = (\\n            options.max_width\\n            if self.width is None\", \"new_text\": \"            Padding(self.renderable, _padding) if any(_padding) else self.renderable\\n        )\\n        style = console.get_style(self.style)\\n        border_style = style + console.get_style(self.border_style)\\n        width = (\\n            options.max_width\\n            if self.width is None\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in rich/panel.py (hunk at line 205).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"rich/panel.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n        title_text = self._title\\n        if title_text is not None:\\n            title_text.stylize_before(partial_border_style)\\n\\n        child_width = (\\n            width - 2\", \"new_text\": \"\\n        title_text = self._title\\n        if title_text is not None:\\n            title_text.stylize_before(border_style)\\n\\n        child_width = (\\n            width - 2\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in rich/panel.py (hunk at line 254).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"rich/panel.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n        subtitle_text = self._subtitle\\n        if subtitle_text is not None:\\n            subtitle_text.stylize_before(partial_border_style)\\n\\n        if subtitle_text is None or width <= 4:\\n            yield Segment(box.get_bottom([width - 2]), border_style)\", \"new_text\": \"\\n        subtitle_text = self._subtitle\\n        if subtitle_text is not None:\\n            subtitle_text.stylize_before(border_style)\\n\\n        if subtitle_text is None or width <= 4:\\n            yield Segment(box.get_bottom([width - 2]), border_style)\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Re-running the repro after the edit to check the fix.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_rich_3718.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "PASS: repro script now succeeds (no failure output after the fix)."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Repro passes. Now the narrowest relevant tests.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_com