ines per call.\n   Use the graph-navigation skill for the exact procedure.\n3. REPRODUCE FIRST. Before editing anything, write a small script\n   under /tmp that triggers the reported failure, and run it with\n   run_command. Confirm you see the reported failure. If you cannot\n   reproduce it, your localization is wrong: go back to step 2. Use\n   the reproduce-first skill for the exact procedure.\n4. FIX. Make one small edit at a time with edit_file (prefer it over\n   write_file, which rewrites whole files). Re-run the /tmp repro\n   after each edit. One hypothesis at a time: if a fix does not change\n   the repro outcome, revert it before trying the next idea.\n5. VERIFY (narrow to wide). Run the narrowest relevant test first\n   (single test, quiet, short traceback), then the containing test\n   file, then the affected package directory. After every pytest run,\n   use the test-summary skill: never paste raw pytest output into\n   your reasoning, condense it to a short failure summary first.\n   Stop expanding the test scope once the repro passes and the\n   directly related tests pass.\n6. CLEAN AND SUBMIT. Delete any scratch files under /workspace (there\n   should be none), run get_status to confirm the diff touches only\n   library code, then call submit_patch. get_status and submit_patch\n   are free and do not count toward the tool-call budget.\n\n## Budget discipline\n\n- You have about 5 minutes and about 50 tool calls per task. Poll\n  get_status every 8-10 calls. If fewer than 10 calls remain, stop\n  exploring and submit the best patch you have.\n- If the same edit fails 3 times, or the same test fails 3 times with\n  no change, stop and submit the best patch instead of looping.\n- Keep the context small: short reads, short repro output, summarized\n  test output. The context ceiling is 32,768 tokens and a flooded\n  context is a failed task."}, {"role": "user", "content": "\u2728 Add support for `app.frontend(\"/\", directory=\"dist\")` and `router.frontend(\"/\", directory=\"dist\")`\n\n## Pull Request\r\n\r\n\u2728 Add support for `app.frontend(\"/\", directory=\"dist\")` and `router.frontend(\"/\", directory=\"dist\")`\r\n\r\n<!--\r\nPlease start with a GitHub Discussion.\r\n\r\nOnce a team member asks you to open a PR, create it and link the discussion here.\r\n\r\nObvious typo fixes can be made in a PR without starting a discussion.\r\n-->\r\n\r\nDiscussion: <!-- Link to the GitHub Discussion -->\r\n\r\n## Description\r\n\r\n<!-- Write the description of your PR here -->\r\n\r\n## AI Disclaimer\r\n\r\nCodex with GPT 5.5, long design iterations, then many iterations tweaking and improving the implementation. Then some refactors and docs manually written as well.\r\n\r\n<!-- If using AI, write here the prompt and model used -->\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>AI transcript</summary>\r\n\r\n<!-- Paste here the entire AI transcript -->\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n## Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] This PR is an obvious typo fix, or it links to a GitHub Discussion for the proposed code change.\r\n- [ ] I added tests for the change.\r\n- [ ] The new or updated tests fail on the main branch and pass on this PR.\r\n- [ ] Coverage stays at 100%.\r\n- [ ] The documentation explains the change if needed.\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/routing.py (hunk at line 826).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/routing.py\", \"old_text\": \"\\n_FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY = \\\"fastapi\\\"\\n_FASTAPI_EFFECTIVE_ROUTE_CONTEXT_KEY = \\\"effective_route_context\\\"\\n_FASTAPI_INCLUDED_ROUTER_KEY = \\\"included_router\\\"\\n_effective_route_context_var: ContextVar[Any | None] = ContextVar(\\n    \\\"fastapi_effective_route_context\\\", default=None\\n)\\n_SCOPE_MISSING = object()\\n\\n\\ndef _get_fastapi_scope(scope: Scope) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    fastapi_scope = scope.setdefault(_FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY, {})\\n    assert isinstance(fastapi_scope, dict)\\n    return fastapi_scope\\n\\n\\ndef _get_scope_effective_route_context(scope: Scope) -> Any | None:\\n    return scope.get(_FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY, {}).get(_FASTAPI_EFFECTIVE_ROUTE_CONTEXT_KEY)\\n\", \"new_text\": \"\\n_FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY = \\\"fastapi\\\"\\n_FASTAPI_EFFECTIVE_ROUTE_CONTEXT_KEY = \\\"effective_route_context\\\"\\n_FASTAPI_FRONTEND_PATH_KEY = \\\"frontend_path\\\"\\n_FASTAPI_INCLUDED_ROUTER_KEY = \\\"included_router\\\"\\n_effective_route_context_var: ContextVar[Any | None] = ContextVar(\\n    \\\"fastapi_effective_route_context\\\", default=None\\n)\\n_SCOPE_MISSING = object()\\n\\n\\nclass _RouteWithPath(Protocol):\\n    path: str\\n\\n\\ndef _get_fastapi_scope(scope: Scope) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    fastapi_scope = scope.setdefault(_FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY, {})\\n    assert isinstance(fastapi_scope, dict)\\n    return fastapi_scope\\n\\n\\ndef _update_scope(scope: Scope, child_scope: Scope) -> None:\\n    fastapi_child_scope = child_scope.get(_FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY)\\n    for key, value in child_scope.items():\\n        if key != _FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY:\\n            scope[key] = value\\n    if isinstance(fastapi_child_scope, dict):\\n        _get_fastapi_scope(scope).update(fastapi_child_scope)\\n\\n\\ndef _get_scope_effective_route_context(scope: Scope) -> Any | None:\\n    return scope.get(_FASTAPI_SCOPE_KEY, {}).get(_FASTAPI_EFFECTIVE_ROUTE_CONTEXT_KEY)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}], "metadata": {"source": "programmatic", "instance_id": "fastapi_15800", "repo": "fastapi/fastapi", "base_commit": "f1d750fddad90e2faad6c3cc5c85c7687b787e89", "files": ["docs_src/frontend/tutorial001_py310.py", "docs_src/frontend/tutorial002_py310.py", "docs_src/frontend/tutorial003_py310.py", "docs_src/frontend/tutorial004_py310.py", "docs_src/frontend/tutorial005_py310.py", "docs_src/frontend/tutorial006_py310.py", "fastapi/applications.py", "fastapi/routing.py"], "symbols": ["add_api_route", "frontend", "api_route", "matches"], "n_hunks": 20, "n_files": 8, "stripped_hunks": 0, "lossy_hunks": 6, "test_target": ["te