=True`\n\n\ud83d\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True`\r\n\r\nRelated to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussions/14184, https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/issues/14483\r\n\r\n"}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Before editing anything, I'll write a small repro script under /tmp that triggers the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"write_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"/tmp/repro_fastapi_14482.py\", \"content\": \"\\\"\\\"\\\"Repro for fastapi_14482 (programmatic replay; generic script).\\\"\\\"\\\"\\nimport sys\\nsys.path.insert(0, \\\"/workspace\\\")\\n\\nfrom fastapi._compat.v2 import ModelField  # noqa: F401\\n\\n# Reported failure (from the issue):\\n# \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` \\ud83d\\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` Related to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussi...\\n# A faithful repro needs the exact failing call from the issue, so\\n# this script confirms the module imports and the symbol exists;\\n# the failure itself is triggered from the issue's example.\\nprint(\\\"repro ready:\\\", ModelField)\\n\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "File written."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Running the repro to confirm the reported failure.\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"run_command\", \"arguments\": {\"command\": \"python /tmp/repro_fastapi_14482.py\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "FAIL: \ud83d\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` \ud83d\udc1b Fix handling arbitrary types when using `arbitrary_types_allowed=True` Related to https://github.com/fastapi/fastapi/discussi..."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/_compat/v2.py (hunk at line 1).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/_compat/v2.py\", \"old_text\": \"import re\\nimport warnings\\nfrom copy import 