`\r\n\r\nWhen trying to use a `pydantic.v1` model with FastAPI, an error is raised."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/openapi/utils.py (hunk at line 262).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"    operation_ids: set[str],\\n    model_name_map: ModelNameMap,\\n    field_mapping: dict[\\n        tuple[ModelField, Literal[\\\"validation\\\", \\\"serialization\\\"]], JsonSchemaValue\\n    ],\\n    separate_input_output_schemas: bool = True,\\n) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any]]:\", \"new_text\": \"    operation_ids: set[str],\\n    model_name_map: ModelNameMap,\\n    field_mapping: dict[\\n        tuple[ModelField, Literal[\\\"validation\\\", \\\"serialization\\\"]], dict[str, Any]\\n    ],\\n    separate_input_output_schemas: bool = True,\\n) -> tuple[dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any], dict[str, Any]]:\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/openapi/utils.py (hunk at line 454).\n<|tool_call|>{\"name\": \"edit_file\", \"arguments\": {\"path\": \"fastapi/openapi/utils.py\", \"old_text\": \"            route, routing.APIRoute\\n        ):\\n            if route.body_field:\\n                assert _is_model_field(route.body_field), (\\n                    \\\"A request body must be a Pydantic Field\\\"\\n                )\\n                body_fields_from_routes.append(route.body_field)\", \"new_text\": \"            route, routing.APIRoute\\n        ):\\n            if route.body_field:\\n                assert isinstance(route.body_field, ModelField), (\\n                    \\\"A request body must be a Pydantic Field\\\"\\n                )\\n                body_fields_from_routes.append(route.body_field)\"}}<|tool_call_end|>"}, {"role": "user", "content": "Edit applied."}, {"role": "assistant", "content": "Applying the fix in fastapi/param_functions.py 